# D1 for keel issue #126: golang/go CL 803220 patch set 1 executed on amd64, which its
# reporter could not do. Verbatim output of the detached run keel-d1b-803220-ps1-antares,
# 2026-09-02. This comment block is the ONLY addition; everything below it is the run's own
# stdout as written to the gitignored build/d1b-803220-ps1-antares.log.
#
# Host: antares.local, AMD RYZEN AI MAX+ 395 w/ Radeon 8060S, 32 threads, linux/amd64,
# GOAMD64=v1, bootstrap go1.27.0. This arm needs no quiet-host discipline: it is a
# correctness test, not a measurement.
#
# Revisions, fetched at depth 2 so the CL and its parent arrive together:
#   ps1  ecafbe48e206bd28e53385cb78e4448e1a5eb1b5  CL 803220/1, Junyang Shao, 2026-07-20
#   base e36c20c7a55b0b77a5dbbfe84641f2f0dd84c0b0  its parent, the control revision
#   git diff --stat base ps1 = licm.go +73/-1, licm_test.go +57 -- exactly the CL.
#
# The repro, which is the whole of it. The driver lived in /tmp rather than scripts/ (the
# apparatus cap has no paid session to spend against this month), so the commands are
# recorded here instead and this file is the reproducible record:
#
#   git init && git remote add origin https://go.googlesource.com/go
#   git fetch --depth=2 origin refs/changes/20/803220/1
#   git checkout -f ecafbe48e206bd28e53385cb78e4448e1a5eb1b5     # and, in a copy, its parent
#   ( cd src && GOROOT_BOOTSTRAP=/usr/local/go bash make.bash )  # once per revision
#   cd src/cmd/compile/internal/amd64
#   GOEXPERIMENT=simd ../../../../../bin/go list -f '{{.TestGoFiles}} {{.XTestGoFiles}}' .
#   GOEXPERIMENT=simd ../../../../../bin/go test -count=1 -v -run 'TestGoAMD64v1|TestLoop' .
#
# Three arms, and the third is why the second is evidence:
#   ARM1 base           rc=0  PASS   -- the license: the test passes at the control revision
#   ARM2 ps1            rc=1  FAIL   -- the finding: SIGTRAP in testLoop3 at versions_simd_test.go:31
#   ARM3 base+unguarded rc=1  FAIL   -- the instrument control, where NONZERO is the pass
#
# ARM3 is testLoop3's body with `if !archsimd.X86.AVX2()` removed and nothing else changed;
# without it, a green ARM2 could not be told apart from a harness that cannot see a fault at
# all. Its clobber tally is ARM1's plus exactly one more of each of the four avx2 opcodes,
# which is an independent witness that the control is the loop it claims to be.
#
# A first run (build/d1-803220-ps1-antares.log, kept) reported all three arms rc=9 UNMEASURED:
# its guard read `.TestGoFiles`, and these tests are `package amd64_test`, so they are an
# external test package and live in `.XTestGoFiles`. The guard failed closed on its own defect.
# Run 2 therefore controls the guard both ways before scoring any arm -- GOEXPERIMENT=simd must
# show versions_simd_test.go, GOEXPERIMENT=none must show versions_nosimd_test.go and not the
# simd one -- because a checker that returns the same answer in both worlds is not a checker.
#
driver: 2026-09-02T04:18:02Z  host=antares.local  script=d1b.sh
